<h3 id=3D"complexity-analysis">Complexity Analysis</h3>
<p><strong>Time complexity:</strong> The time complexity of <code>find_the_=
median_from_two_sorted_arrays</code> is <span class=3D"katex"><span class=
=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><seman=
tics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>=E2=81=A1=
</mo><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mo stretch=
y=3D"false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo separator=3D"true">,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stre=
tchy=3D"false">)</mo><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo><mo stretchy=3D"false">)<=
/mo></mrow><annotation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">O(\log(min(m,n)))</an=
notation></semantics></math></span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=
=3D"true"><span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height: 1em; =
vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal" style=3D"m=
argin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class=3D"mopen">(</span><span class=
=3D"mop">lo<span style=3D"margin-right: 0.01389em;">g</span></span><span cl=
ass=3D"mopen">(</span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal">min</span><span class=
=3D"mopen">(</span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal">m</span><span class=3D"m=
punct">,</span><span class=3D"mspace" style=3D"margin-right: 0.1667em;"></s=
pan><span class=3D"mord mathnormal">n</span><span class=3D"mclose">)))</spa=
n></span></span></span> because we perform binary search over the smaller o=
f the two input arrays.</p>
<p><strong>Space complexity:</strong> The space complexity is <span class=
=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/19=
98/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><mn=
>1</mn><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=3D"applicat=
ion/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=3D"katex-=
html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=
=3D"height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class=3D"mord mathn=
ormal" style=3D"margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class=3D"mopen">(</=
span><span class=3D"mord">1</span><span class=3D"mclose">)</span></span></s=
pan></span>.</p>
<p><em>Note: this explanation refers to the two middle values as "median va=
lues" to keep things simple. However, it's important to understand that the=
